{
  "version": 1,
  "about": "Golden cases for the Jellyfin and Emby connect screens (the sign-in redesign, Apple TV 1.0.28). Read by scripts/nostalgex-signin-smoke.mjs (scripts/nostalgex-signin.js, web tuner and Docker; npm run test:signin). Written from Nostalgex/NostalgexTests/SignInFlowTests.swift and ServerURLNormalizerTests.swift and the spec in the Apple TV app, so a Swift test (ServerURLNormalizer.candidates, LANServerDiscovery.parse and dedupe, SignInFlow.outcome, parsePublicInfo, parseQuickConnectEnabled, parsePublicUsers, preferredMethod, offersQuickConnect) and the Roku port can read the same file. Bodies are the raw text a server sends. null means none (no server, can't say).",
  "candidates": [
    {
      "raw": "192.0.2.10",
      "out": [
        "http://192.0.2.10:8096",
        "http://192.0.2.10"
      ],
      "about": "a bare IP tries Jellyfin's and Emby's 8096 first"
    },
    {
      "raw": "http://192.0.2.10:8096/web/#/home",
      "out": [
        "http://192.0.2.10:8096"
      ],
      "about": "an address copied from the web UI"
    },
    {
      "raw": "http://nas.local:8096/web/index.html#!/home",
      "out": [
        "http://nas.local:8096"
      ]
    },
